{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03427",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.2,
      "end_seconds": 2.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Good afternoon, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.25,
      "end_seconds": 9.37,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "So, yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 10.84,
      "end_seconds": 16.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "hmm, good morning, doctor i came along to help out"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.98,
      "end_seconds": 23.05,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Right, of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.16,
      "end_seconds": 29.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "It's sudden breathlessness five days after surgery, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.96,
      "end_seconds": 31.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.05,
      "end_seconds": 36.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "I've had it for two months"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.57,
      "end_seconds": 39.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "How frequently does it come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.12,
      "end_seconds": 58.51,
      "duration_seconds": 14.39,
      "text": "it just comes and goes. And sharp chest pain on breathing in, too. As for sharp chest pain on breathing in, severe, really. It comes and goes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.73,
      "end_seconds": 71.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "A few quick ones: wound problem, fever or coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.45,
      "end_seconds": 78.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "I mean, no, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.05,
      "end_seconds": 82.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Okay, has your heart given you any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.18,
      "end_seconds": 89.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Yeah, you know, no, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.9,
      "end_seconds": 93.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "so, anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.26,
      "end_seconds": 98.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "I mean, no, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.97,
      "end_seconds": 107.91,
      "duration_seconds": 7.94,
      "text": "what conditions have you been treated for in the past? I ask because it helps me narrow things down"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.18,
      "end_seconds": 111.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "I've got acid reflux."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.44,
      "end_seconds": 132.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.54,
      "end_seconds": 137.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "I don't think I have any, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.56,
      "end_seconds": 139.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.49,
      "end_seconds": 148.07,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.68,
      "end_seconds": 151.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.07,
      "end_seconds": 157.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.1,
      "end_seconds": 161.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.19,
      "end_seconds": 166.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.83,
      "end_seconds": 168.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "tell me about your eating"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.01,
      "end_seconds": 177.41,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.41,
      "end_seconds": 182.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.95,
      "end_seconds": 190.07,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "I mean, I'm on omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.69,
      "end_seconds": 192.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.53,
      "end_seconds": 205.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "that's it, just a a little longer.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.04,
      "end_seconds": 229.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.14,
      "text": "Okay: respiratory rate 22, blood pressure 132 over 82, pulse is 90 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.14,
      "end_seconds": 232.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.34,
      "end_seconds": 236.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "I'll come back to the numbers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.85,
      "end_seconds": 241.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.77,
      "end_seconds": 243.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.79,
      "end_seconds": 246.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "nearly finished here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.2,
      "end_seconds": 259.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "Your left calf is swollen and tender and and your oxygen is low."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.37,
      "end_seconds": 273.23,
      "duration_seconds": 10.86,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. So, based on the history and the examination, this is probably a possible blood clot in the lung after surgery."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.05,
      "end_seconds": 318.67,
      "duration_seconds": 26.62,
      "text": "I think a CT pulmonary angiogram makes sense here, for possible pulmonary embolus. You'll be taking enoxaparin, 1.5 mg per kg, once now, single dose. That should help with possible clot. Please go to to hospital now, I will call ahead. I'll also refer you to the emergency team. Let's review you straight away. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.02,
      "end_seconds": 321.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    }
  ]
}